# Branches almost always add entries to the same place in the changelog — the
# top of the unreleased section — so every parallel pull request conflicts
# there, over text where both sides are simply wanted. Git's built-in "union"
# driver resolves such a conflict by keeping both sides' lines instead of
# writing conflict markers.
#
# It is deliberately scoped to this one file: union merging prose would happily
# produce duplicated sentences. Entries can still land in an odd order or
# under a heading that was added on one side only, so read the result of a
# merge that touched the changelog before pushing it.
CHANGELOG.md merge=union
